<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12620"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, April 03, 2005 - 11:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I must say right now that I am open-minded about the possibility of a Zodiac connection between the double murders last year in Napa and Sonoma - Leslie Mazzara and Adriane Insogna in the former, Leslie Cutshall and Jason Allen the latter - meaning that while I have to wonder that if Z is still alive he may have done these things to show BTK yet again &#34;how it&#39;s done,&#34; I still maintain the possibility in my mind that Zodiac is dead. To me this superposition of possibilities is crucial to maintaining, I don&#39;t know, intellectual honesty. We live in a society that abhors the changing of one&#39;s mind, and frankly, I hate that. Intellectual flexibility is a hallmark of intelligence, to me, and only current political rhetoric has converted this flexibility into something negative. <BR> <BR>To that end, I had to go back and examine the following Doe network file - <a href="http://www.doenetwork.us/cases/454umoh.html">case no. 454UMOH</a>. <BR> <BR>It prompted me to do the following; <a href="http://www.planethuff.com/darkside/archives/ZODIACCHANDLER.JPG">Zodiac Suspect drawing/Joseph Chandler age-regression/Actual photo of &#34;Chandler.&#34;</a> <BR> <BR>I&#39;d like opinions on this. I&#39;d be posting this at Zodiackiller, but haven&#39;t received my registration for the site yet. <BR> <BR>My personal opinion is best relayed by my wife&#39;s words on looking at the comparison I made; <i>&#34;The Zodiac drawing looks more like that guy might have looked when he was young than the drawing beside his photo.&#34;</i> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
