<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12672"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 05, 2005 - 12:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->HeY Steve, since we are working on both cases, can I get you and the others to do a 60&#39;s 70&#39;s  culture profile for us. My thinking is muli leveled at the moment, connecting Rader to Z, and Z to Others, I have stumbled on something odd. Rader was into bondage, I found Sharon Tate who I knew was in porn, in a bondage pic, before Mansion had her killed. M. Hedge, lived in her old house I think,Howard has a site that Tom added to about Mansion and Z.  There is a motorcycle club in Cali with the born to kill that kidnap and sell children still waiting for that link. My point is that if we have the background of the times all these nuts were out. we may be able to cut thru some of the searches. Thanks Sheila<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12672-->
<!--Post: 12981--><!--Time: 1113914135-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12981"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 19, 2005 - 5:35 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->As I have taken the time recently to analyze the comparisons between Zodiac and BTK. I find in my notes that they are two entirly seperate types of personalities. Forgive me if this was obvious to everyone else from the start. I Have noticed the strict thinking patterns in Z&#39;s character. As Rader&#39;s personality is made up of free flow undetermined thought patterns. IMO In order for someone like Zodiac to stay focused in day life. He had to have order, This &#34;order&#34; was his control in society. He worked at jobs that required counting, or a lot of things to shuffle around like for example, Inventory. I may have also been his job in the military. I was a storekeeper in the Navy and this is what we did. Everything we did had a book, from start to finish, and if you followed everything by the book, you would succeed. Rader on the other hand has a creative style. A full rich fantisy life. He tried to copy Z, but could not think as Z does. This is obvious when you look at his poems and puzzles. They are simplified versions of something Z might have been capable of doing when he was a child. Rader knowing that Z was all about controling his environment tried to copy this pattern at home, at work,  In his need for &#34;power&#34; because somewhere in his mind he thought that was why Zodiac killed, Or it is possible that Rader saw the power the Zodiac Killer had over people. So he naturally assumed that it was Zodiac&#39;s intention. Rader&#39;s first mistake was trying to copy someone else&#39;s ideas. IMO he will be just another Z copycat. The difference between the two? Zodiac lived this mindset, everyday, everywhere he went he was looking for the next step. Following the patterns, counting. Rader spent more time being a normal family man. He enjoyed killing first, then came the identity. As we all now know, his identity only included the killer when it served his purpose.   Thanks Sheila<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12981-->
<!--Post: 13149--><!--Time: 1114310885-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13149"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 23, 2005 - 7:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->E-It seems that Zodiac&#39;s letters were more hatefully directed at LE, than BTK&#39;s. Meaning - it appeared that his intent when writing was to piss off LE, whereas BTK&#39;s intent was taunting with clue based ramblings. This is my first impression, I just looked at them recently. <BR> <BR>Do you all think that he is still alive? You would think that LE putting that case on the back burner would really motivate him to come out.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13149-->
<!--Post: 13153--><!--Time: 1114321020-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13153"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 23, 2005 - 10:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rocky, I am really not sure at this point. I feel IMO that his is still alive. I have just begun to learn all the details that others have been collecting over the years concerning Zodiac. I have a feeling that If his is able and is still alive that he will contact someone in this next year. Due to the New Movie I have heard about. I agree that he was angry with LE, but more so for not geting his information right than anything else. He was smart in his ideas and wanted the public to know it. When LE would make comments that he felt were untrue or did not relay his unique thinking &#40;IE Flashlight taped to gun&#41; He was quick to correct them. I feel that Rader was Mean, he liked killing just to do it. He hated cops and any type of authority that he was not in control of. But yet sane enough to control his actions when needed. Showing me he was a fake. zodiac on the other hand is really insane. Everything he did was for his narc. personality of ensuring he had slaves in the afterlife. In the begining of his killing I am begining to think he chose his victims based on what he would need in the afterlife. A pretty Cheerleader, A waitress, an Athlete, a driver, Etc. Each to serve as a different function in his Paradise. If you read Elizabeth Bathory stories you will see her husband was just as nuts as she was. When he would come home from battle he would pour honey on the servents and tie them to ant hills. Things that zodiac has mentioned doing to his victims in the afterlife. Zodiac was once a semi-normal person. Then he was &#34;transformed&#34; Rader could ape his actions but never be as &#34;out there&#34; as Zodiac. I think when zodiac almost got caught, at the time of Paul Stein&#39;s murder he got scared. That is why he went into hiding and may have continued to kill but without laying claim to more victims. Rader is now saying he is sorry. I doubt Zodiac would know that word. I also think Zodiac was like Bundy, Jack the Ripper, etc. He was way before his time. These types of personalities where unheard of before modern science, and modern day killers. I watched a movie once about Jack The Riper, In the movie he was a &#34;Time Traveler&#34; going back in time to kill. The concept makes sense. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13153-->
<!--Post: 13214--><!--Time: 1114550465-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13214"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 26, 2005 - 2:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have written <a href="http://www.planethuff.com/darkside/archives/000684.html">another blog entry</a> about <a href="http://www.doenetwork.us/cases/454umoh.html">John Doe 454umoh</a>, as a mysterious blogger named <a href="http://xymphora.blogspot.com/2005/04/was-joe-chandler-zodiac.html">xymphora found a new potential connection</a> between Z and Ohio...the unsolved murders between 1979 and 1982 of 8 people between Akron, Toledo, and Logan. This would have been about the time John Doe, going by the name Joseph Chandler, arrived in Ohio. <BR> <BR>The victims were all couples, just like, with the exception of Paul Stine, all of Zodiac&#39;s victims. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13214-->
<!--Post: 13251--><!--Time: 1114655879-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13251"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, April 27, 2005 - 7:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Interesting Steve. If I had his birthday I would be able to tell you all about him. I am doing other serial killers charts right now. Can you post the details of the murders here for us to look at. The MO, or the links to them?  Thanks Sheila<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13251-->
<!--Post: 13254--><!--Time: 1114664829-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13254"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, April 27, 2005 - 10:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Do you guys think he had a military background? I keep going back to the watch that was found at a crime scene.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13254-->
<!--Post: 13256--><!--Time: 1114667865-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13256"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, April 27, 2005 - 10:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rocky, if you mean Zodiac - I think we can reliably say BTK did have one - yes. I think he was a navy man. Partly because some of the symbols he used for his ciphers could be found in various navy handbooks on meteorology and cryptography.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13256-->
<!--Post: 13271--><!--Time: 1114734904-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13271"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 28, 2005 - 5:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Steve sorry dear, I was referring to Zodiac. His symbols were very unique. Did you get the disciphering from the guy that originally broke it?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13271-->
<!--Post: 13272--><!--Time: 1114735723-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13272"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 28, 2005 - 5:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rocky, I am not sure what you mean about the symbols Only one of the cipers was ever broken and Sean and I are working on the other one. From scratch.  The symbols don&#39;t really mean that much, they just represent a letter. They are symbols to confuse us. Or go along with the Zodaic Idea. I think he was in the military. But no one really knows for sure. But No, everything we are doing now. Comes out of our head. I can not allow myself to get buried in all the theories so I worked on the code before ever reading the Z site. We are trying a new approach. I hope that answers your question. Your Friend Sheila<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13272-->
<!--Post: 13275--><!--Time: 1114736536-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13275"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 28, 2005 - 6:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->E-I&#39;m referring to the way Donald Harden and his wife disciphered Zodiac&#39;s letters. It&#39;s on Tom&#39;s website. If you guys are doing this from scratch, have a ball! I&#39;d love to know what you come up with. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13275-->
<!--Post: 13281--><!--Time: 1114769021-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13281"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 29, 2005 - 3:03 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->No, I have gotten the origin of the symbols from numerous sources. Harden and his wife didn&#39;t know what the actual symbols came from, they simply worked off of smart assumptions about the possible content of the message and from there their method was in part some kind of frequency analysis.  <BR> <BR>I think that even though he may have culled the symbols from books on weather charts and semaphore such as is used to bring planes in on an aircraft carrier, Z threw out the symbols&#39; original uses completely and simply made himself a cipher alphabet by his own lights. Knowing the origins of the symbols may not be as informative as we&#39;d think.  <BR> <BR>I cannot say, no one can truly say they are 100% sure Z was navy, but it&#39;s a stronger possibility than other branches due to his shoe type, in part, and the use of some of those symbols. &#40;Semaphore, for instance.&#41; <BR> <BR>I think solving a cipher is a fascinating exercise, but Z was all about the game, a quality Denny shared. I can&#39;t believe he was stupid enough to think there was no possibility his puzzles would ever be solved. The solutions to the unsolved ones will be just as infuriatingly uninformative as the solution to the one Harden and his wife solved.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13281-->
<!--Post: 13291--><!--Time: 1114818957-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13291"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 29, 2005 - 4:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rocky, Go over to The Z site and look under The ciper thread for 340. There you will find my solution. I agree with Steve and that of course was what I was trying to say. but My head was on backwards at the time. I looked at Harden&#39;s solution and it is great. The problem was that no Two Z ciphers are alike. So I had to start from scratch and forget the symbols. Sorry If I didn&#39;t explain. Your Friend Sheila<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13291-->
